class.description:
A script implemented in the GDScript programming language, saved with the [code].gd[/code] extension. The script extends the functionality of all objects that instantiate it.
Calling [method new] creates a new instance of the script. [method Object.set_script] extends an existing object, if that object's class matches one of the script's base classes.
If you are looking for GDScript's built-in functions, see [@GDScript] instead.
[b]Strict type analysis:[/b] GDScript supports nullable annotations, typed callable and signal signatures, and nested typed containers. Nullable object types use [code]T?[/code], while plain [code]T[/code] can be checked as non-nullable when [member ProjectSettings.debug/gdscript/analysis/strict_null_checks] is enabled. [Callable] and [Signal] signatures can be written as [code]Callable[[ArgType, ...], ReturnType][/code] and [code]Signal[[ArgType, ...]][/code]. [Array] and [Dictionary] annotations can contain nested typed containers such as [code]Dictionary[String, Array[int]][/code].
[codeblock]
signal renamed_to(new_name: String)

func get_target() -> Node?:
	return null

func accept_target(target: Node) -> void:
	pass

func name_length(name: String) -> int:
	return name.length()

func on_renamed(new_name: String) -> void:
	pass

func get_dynamic_value() -> Variant:
	return 1

func use_strict_types() -> void:
	var maybe_target: Node? = get_target()
	if maybe_target != null:
		accept_target(maybe_target)

	var callback: Callable[[String], int] = name_length
	var length: int = callback.call("Player")

	var renamed: Signal[[String]] = renamed_to
	renamed.connect(on_renamed)
	renamed.emit("Player")

	var scores: Dictionary[String, Array[int]] = {
		"level_1": [10, 20, 30],
	}
	print(length, scores["level_1"][0])

	# Rejected when strict_null_checks is enabled:
	# accept_target(get_target())

	# Rejected when strict_dynamic_checks is enabled:
	# var typed_value: int = get_dynamic_value()
[/codeblock]
Most callable and signal signature checks run as part of normal static analysis. [member ProjectSettings.debug/gdscript/analysis/strict_dynamic_checks] adds stricter checks at dynamic boundaries by rejecting [Variant] values where a non-[Variant] static type is required.

method.description:
Returns a new instance of the script.
[codeblock]
var MyClass = load("myclass.gd")
var instance = MyClass.new()
print(instance.get_script() == MyClass) # Prints true
[/codeblock]
